index 4479b53..903a2c3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,47 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Browser agent tools (WebMCP)
+
+The shared header exposes client-side tools using React's `useWebMCP` integration
+and the current `document.modelContext` API. Registration is feature-detected;
+browsers without WebMCP retain the normal search and reading-list UI. Tool
+registrations are removed with an AbortSignal when their React islands unmount,
+including during Astro client navigation.
+
+| Tool | Input | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | `{ query: string }` | Search titles and summaries; return article metadata and links. |
+| `get_reading_list` | `{}` | Return the visitor's saved slugs and article metadata. |
+| `set_article_saved` | `{ slug: string, saved: boolean }` | Set the desired saved state and update visible bookmarks. |
+| `read_current_article` | `{}` | Return the displayed article's title, body text and URL; available on article pages. |
+| `get_article_popularity` | `{ id: string }` | Query article popularity on article pages. |
+| `get_plant_stats` | `{}` | Query plant statistics on “The Silent Architects of Earth.” |
+| `get_tide_levels` | `{}` | Query the tide service on “The Coastal Pulse.” |
+| `get_coffee_brew_status` | `{}` | Query the brewing service on “The Global Alchemy of Coffee.” |
+| `open_article_search` | `{}` | Open the search flyout, making `search_articles_form` discoverable. |
+| `open_reading_list` | `{}` | Open the reading-list flyout, making `update_reading_list_form` discoverable. |
+
+The forms use `toolname`, `tooldescription` and `toolautosubmit`, labeled named
+controls, and native validation. Agent submissions receive JSON results through
+`SubmitEvent.respondWith()` without navigating away. Manual submissions use the
+same handlers. Saving is reversible and idempotent: retrying `saved: true` keeps
+an article saved. The reading-list endpoint still supports legacy toggle calls
+that omit `saved`.
+
+Article utility tools preserve the demo services’ HTTP failures and redirect details;
+they do not change the intentional network-debugging scenarios.
+
+WebMCP requires a supporting browser and a secure context (HTTPS or localhost).
+See the [WebMCP specification](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/) for
+current API availability. For an in-page consumer in a supporting browser:
+
+```js
+const tools = await document.modelContext.getTools();
+const search = tools.find(tool => tool.name === 'search_articles');
+const result = await document.modelContext.executeTool(search, { query: 'coffee' });
+```
+
+Run `pnpm test:tools` for isolated client-tool checks and `pnpm build` for the
+production build. These checks do not start a server or import a server entrypoint.
